French astronaut Sophie Adenot is to leave the International Space Station again on Tuesday for a second time, a week after she became the first French woman to perform a spacewalk.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d50039fa-9fc2-11f1-b33b-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:57:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg">© NASA via Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine's allies pledge to continue support with focus on air defence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-ukraine-s-allies-pledge-to-continue-support-with-focus-on-air-defence</link><description>
Ukraine's allies on Monday pledged to keep up their support in the war against Russia, with a renewed focus on air defence investment to counter a shortage of US Patriot interceptors. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9103d0e-9fe5-11f1-8ca1-af870d26e276</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:17:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/71afd38c-9fa5-11f1-af79-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236363361580.jpg">© Henry Nicholls / Pool AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Saudi Arabia to invest $7 bn in theme parks near Paris: French presidency</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-saudi-arabia-to-invest-7-bn-in-theme-parks-near-paris-french-presidency</link><description>
France and Saudi Arabia on Monday signed a memorandum of understanding for a six-billion-euro ($7 billion) Saudi investment to create three theme parks near Paris, including one likely to be manga-themed, the office of the French president said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5e83b10-9fe6-11f1-a438-af870d26e276</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:08:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4cc18b4-9fe6-11f1-bfdc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e5bef9e73595ec0265cbf9aa320acbe08d2c098a.jpg">© LOU BENOIST / POOL/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Mediterranean migrant rescue ships threatened by Libyan groups, warns NGO</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260824-mediterranean-migrant-rescue-ships-threatened-by-libyan-groups-warns-ngo</link><description>
A leading group monitoring and providing aid to migrants crossing the Mediterranean have warned that its rescue ships have been facing increasing threats and harassment from Libyan groups.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/148ae9a0-8059-11f1-9930-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92ZB9ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/148ae9a0-8059-11f1-9930-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92ZB9ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a4727752-9fa5-11f1-a762-d969d98d7dd8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:22:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/148ae9a0-8059-11f1-9930-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-92ZB9ZR.jpg">© Sameer al-Doumy/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Malian PM's visit to Algeria underlines need for mutual security goals</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260824-malian-pm-s-visit-to-algeria-underlines-need-for-mutual-security-goals</link><description>
The acting head of the Malian government, General Abdoulaye Maiga has begun a two-day visit to Algeria. It comes amid a thaw after months of tension. RFI spoke to Bakary Sambe, the Director of the Timbuktu Institute about the security situation and what the countries hope to gain from the meeting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/626a8dea-9fc3-11f1-aa7c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22312578792228-Abdoulaye-Ma%C3%AFga.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/626a8dea-9fc3-11f1-aa7c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22312578792228-Abdoulaye-Ma%C3%AFga.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83603542-9fc1-11f1-8b4e-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:25:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/626a8dea-9fc3-11f1-aa7c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22312578792228-Abdoulaye-Ma%C3%AFga.jpg">AP - Peter Dejong</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Six million Somalis face acute hunger as drought and conflict worsen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260824-six-million-somalis-face-acute-hunger-as-drought-and-conflict-worsen</link><description>
Six million people in Somalia are facing acute hunger, with nearly two million children at emergency levels, as severe drought, conflict and falling humanitarian funding deepen what the UN describes as one of the world’s worst malnutrition crises. Medical charity MSF tells RFI it's sounding the alarm "before it's too late".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/089fa040-9f80-11f1-979d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26232458355606-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/089fa040-9f80-11f1-979d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26232458355606-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9ca8582-9f97-11f1-9ee8-75486ab540dd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:40:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/089fa040-9f80-11f1-979d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26232458355606-1.jpg">©  Farah Abdi Warsameh / AP Photo</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Violence against healthcare workers in DRC hampers Ebola response</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260824-violence-against-healthcare-workers-in-drc-hampers-ebola-response</link><description>
Healthcare workers in the Democratic Republic of Congo have been coming under attack, the United Nations and Red Cross have warned, hampering efforts to stem the spread of the Ebola virus, which is spreading 'exponentially'.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a5c8358-9d67-11f1-b9dd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T085519Z-246925543-RC23HLAKM9NK-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a5c8358-9d67-11f1-b9dd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T085519Z-246925543-RC23HLAKM9NK-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cd402608-9f9f-11f1-896c-8324a3ed262e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:08:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a5c8358-9d67-11f1-b9dd-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T085519Z-246925543-RC23HLAKM9NK-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA.jpg">© Gradel Muyisa Mumbere/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Centre-left Glucksmann enters French presidential race as left tries to unite</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260824-centre-left-glucksmann-enters-french-presidential-race-as-left-tries-to-unite</link><description>
French centre-left politician Raphael Glucksmann has announced his candidacy for next year's presidential election, seeking to challenge hard-left leader Jean-Luc Melenchon to lead France's fractured left, as a campaign increasingly dominated by the far right takes shape.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4365a168-9f83-11f1-8a80-dd78f7da95c3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 06:18:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Scorching summer takes toll on bees and honey harvests in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-scorching-summer-takes-toll-on-bees-and-honey-harvests-in-france</link><description>
France produces 20,000 tonnes of honey each year, but successive heatwaves and persistent drought across Europe this summer are impacting bee populations as flowering plants dry out and colonies struggle to find food. Beekeeper Romain Lacotte and his family farm 1,000 hives in Haute-Corrèze, central France, an area considered one of the country's natural water towers. But even there, he tells RFI, high temperatures and lack of rain are taking their toll.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11563ee0-9ae1-11f1-bfbb-0f799d11d84e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:44:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg">© ASSOCIATED PRESS - Jacquelyn Martin </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC and M23 rebels agree on roadmap for peace in eastern Congo</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-drc-and-m23-rebels-agree-on-roadmap-for-peace-in-eastern-congo</link><description>
The Democratic Republic of Congo government and the M23 rebel group have agreed on a roadmap for peace talks aimed at resolving the protracted conflict in eastern DRC. It marks the latest step in an internationally brokered peace process that has seen the parties make cautious concessions, without ending the fighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8dd2067c-9ef4-11f1-b3c6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177576707008.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8dd2067c-9ef4-11f1-b3c6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177576707008.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">57463c2a-9ef6-11f1-9684-4b4489a4c262</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:00:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8dd2067c-9ef4-11f1-b3c6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177576707008.jpg">© AP Photo/Moses Sawasawa</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Saudi crown prince heads to France as Paris seeks closer Gulf ties</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-saudi-crown-prince-heads-to-france-as-paris-seeks-closer-gulf-ties</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron will host Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman on Sunday for a two-day official visit, as Paris looks to deepen ties with Riyadh against a backdrop of war in the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">128f22b8-9d66-11f1-be58-479c257d485f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 07:05:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg">© AP - Michel Euler </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Mystery elephant deaths in Kenya leave experts divided over cause</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-mystery-elephant-deaths-in-kenya-leave-experts-divided-over-cause</link><description>
Conservationists and Maasai communities are calling for urgent answers as paralysis-like symptoms spread among elephants in Kenya's Amboseli National Park, with competing theories emerging over what is causing their deaths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38c7617a-9bd1-11f1-889b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Genghis-Khan-Elephant-Kenya.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38c7617a-9bd1-11f1-889b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Genghis-Khan-Elephant-Kenya.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6595647c-9bcc-11f1-8fd9-dfc10b227463</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:13:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38c7617a-9bd1-11f1-889b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Genghis-Khan-Elephant-Kenya.jpg">© SIMON MAINA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Togo says it has 'serious' evidence against detained French journalists</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260823-togo-says-it-has-serious-evidence-against-detained-french-journalists</link><description>
Togo's government says it has "serious and consistent evidence" against two French documentary filmmakers detained since July on charges of making false statements. Gaël Mocaër and Sebastian Perez Pezzani were arrested along with their Togolese fixer, Fred Vedomey, and have denied wrongdoing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdddc9cc-9ec9-11f1-9875-e5f10da2b52b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:56:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5bf99606-5008-11eb-ae90-005056a964fe/w:1024/p:16x9/000_Par1348444.jpg">© AFP/EMILE KOUTON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Southern African mothers plead for sons lured to Russia's war in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260823-southern-african-mothers-plead-for-sons-lured-to-russia-s-war</link><description>
Instead of celebrating her son's birthday this month, Zimbabwean mother Rodwin Chitewere spent the day praying for his body to be brought home from Russia, where he was reportedly killed fighting Moscow's war against Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3108037c-9b90-11f1-8781-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/4f0ee42d48be3951fcc0a4d769636323e1b83893.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3108037c-9b90-11f1-8781-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/4f0ee42d48be3951fcc0a4d769636323e1b83893.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a3badee-9bb2-11f1-9818-f5b8caecbf68</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:28:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3108037c-9b90-11f1-8781-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/4f0ee42d48be3951fcc0a4d769636323e1b83893.jpg">© RAJESH JANTILAL / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eroding coastlines unearth and destroy slave graves in French Caribbean</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-eroding-coastlines-unearth-and-destroy-slave-graves-in-french-caribbean</link><description>
Rising seas and coastal erosion are exposing the graves of enslaved people on beaches in the French Caribbean departments of Martinique and Guadeloupe, bringing long-buried remains back into view. Archaeologists say the retreating coastline is revealing new information about people who were enslaved centuries ago, but also destroying sites of historical and cultural importance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a0474c0-9a39-11f1-8ac6-db7960a1f159</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:07:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg">© Thomas Romon / Inrap</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ravaged by wildfires, France's Fontainebleau forest reopens to public</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-france-s-fontainebleau-forest-reopens-to-public-after-wildfires</link><description>
The forest of Fontainebleau outside Paris has partially reopened to the public after remaining off-limits for over a month due to devastating wildfires. From Saturday, visitors can access some 80 percent of the forest, but are being warned to show caution around fragile wildlife and charred trees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b21100-9e04-11f1-bb3d-976fc488f692</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg">© AFP - SIMON WOHLFAHRT </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Still waters run deep: why Palme d'or winner 'Fjord' questions our certainties</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/culture/20260822-why-palme-d-or-winner-fjord-questions-our-certainties-cristian-mungiu-interview</link><description>
An isolated village in Norway sees its peaceful veneer upset by the arrival of a new family in Fjord, the Palme d'Or-winning film released in French cinemas this week. Inspired by real-life cases, Romanian director Cristian Mungiu explores questions of domestic violence, religion, culture and tolerance through a story that asks whose version of the truth can be trusted.
